// Controls of the letter template IDD_LETTER — FR-101, task Т-32-2. A block of their own from
// 1200, contiguous and clear of everything above.
//
// ⚠ **These rectangles are a pool of slots and not a layout.** One template serves five
// letters, each filling a different set of slots, so the position and the height of every
// control below are computed at `WM_INITDIALOG` by `letters::layout` out of the text actually
// put into it, measured with the very `DrawTextW` that will draw it. What the template fixes is
// the *window* — its width, its height and its font — and which slots exist. A slot no letter
// fills is hidden, and a hidden control paints nothing; that is what keeps the rule of the two
// windows above true here as well: **no two owner-drawn statics ever overlap**, because the
// layout assigns disjoint rectangles and hides the rest.
