// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Turkish — `[general] language = "tr"`. LANG_TURKISH 0x1F.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// ⚠ **The dotted and dotless i.** Turkish has four letters where other Latin alphabets have
// two: `i`/`İ` and `ı`/`I`. Every capital at the start of a string below was checked by eye
// against that rule — «İptal», «İstisnalar», «İşlem adı» carry the dot, and «ETKİN DEĞİL» does
// too. Getting it wrong is not mojibake and no instrument catches it; only reading catches it.
